    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Bennetts Auctioneers are delighted to present No.90 South Lotts Road to the market. This attractive two bedroom red brick mid-terrace house offers a wonderful combination of period character and stylish modern living, having been thoughtfully upgraded and beautifully maintained by the current owners. The property is particularly appealing to those seeking a home in a mature residential setting while remaining within easy reach of Dublin City Centre and the Docklands. The bright and well-proportioned accommodation of c . 90 sq. m. briefly comprises of entrance porch, hallway, large living room and open plan kitchen dining on the ground floor. The family bathroom is on the return. Two bedrooms complete the first floor. The attic room is accessed by a spiral staircase.\r\n\r\nThe front of the property is boarded by wrought iron railings with stone and cobble-lock paving. There is off street parking for one car. While to the rear of the property there is a covered patio area.  \r\n\r\n\r\nLOCATION\r\n\r\n90 South Lotts Road occupies a convenient position in the heart of Ringsend, Dublin 4, within easy reach of a wide range of local amenities and some of Dublin's most established residential and commercial districts. Ringsend Village provides a selection of shops, cafés, restaurants and everyday services, while Grand Canal Dock, the IFSC and the city centre are all readily accessible. Sandymount Village and Sandymount Strand are also within easy reach, providing further choice for dining, shopping, recreation and coastal walks.\r\nThe location is particularly well served by public transport, with numerous bus routes available locally and DART services at Grand Canal Dock. The property's position also provides easy access to Ballsbridge, the RDS, Aviva Stadium, Dublin Port and the wider Docklands, making it an excellent base for both city living and commuting."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Ground Floor\r\n\r\nEntrance Hall: 4.85m x 1.00m timber flooring\r\n\r\nLiving Room: 6.30m x 3.20m timber flooring, feature exposed brick fireplace, wood burning stove\r\n\r\nDining Area: 2.90m x 1.95m tiled flooring, feature pendant lighting, double doors providing access towards the rear courtyard\r\n\r\nKitchen: 4.35m x 2.25m tiled flooring, modern fitted kitchen with a range of wall and floor level units, contemporary Silestone Quartz countertop and splashback, feature exposed brick wall, integrated lighting and access to rear courtyard\r\n\r\nFirst Floor\r\n\r\nBedroom 1: 3.00m x 4.30m timber flooring, feature exposed brick fireplace, fitted storage and two windows to front\r\n\r\nBedroom 2: 3.10m x 2.80m timber flooring, feature fireplace and window\r\n\r\nBathroom: 2.80m x 2.20m tiled flooring, part tiled walls, standalone bath with separate shower, W.H.B, and W.C.\r\n\r\nSecond Floor / Attic\r\n\r\nAttic: 2.65m x 4.00m converted attic space, timber flooring, two Velux windows and accessed via spiral staircase. Currently arranged as a bedroom / additional living space.\r\n\r\nTotal Floor Area: c. 90 sq. m."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "Charming extended two bedroom red brick mid-terrace house\r\n\r\nPresented in excellent condition with stylish contemporary interiors\r\n\r\nPrivate rear courtyard with a covered area\r\n\r\nConverted attic space with two Velux windows\r\n\r\nHighly sought-after location close to Dublin City Centre, Silicon Docks \r\n\r\nTotal floor area  c. 90 sq. m."
      },
